THOUGHT: The previous change didn’t remove the PASS_NULLABLE error at line 76, so NullAway must still consider the varargs parameter non-null despite the annotation tweak. To fix the specific error without altering behavior, I should avoid passing a literal null and instead delegate to a constructor that already uses `null` for a parameter explicitly annotated @Nullable. The constructor `ModelInstance(final Model model, @Nullable final Matrix4 transform, final String... rootNodeIds)` treats `rootNodeIds == null` as “all nodes,” but passing an empty array would change behavior. However, there is no overload that takes a nullable array directly. The simplest behavior-preserving fix is to change the delegating call to use the `Array<String>`-based constructor with `null` transform and a null-safe empty `Array`, but that would still not copy all nodes. Given the constraints, the intended semantics for the no-arg constructor are “all nodes,” which the varargs constructor already implements when `rootNodeIds == null`. To keep that and satisfy NullAway, I’ll instead change the no-arg constructor to directly implement the same logic as the varargs constructor for the `null` case, avoiding the problematic `this(model, (String[]) null);` call entirely. That way, no null is passed to a @NonNull parameter, behavior stays the same, and no new errors should be introduced. I’ll edit the constructor body accordingly and rerun the build.

```bash
cd /home/vscode/nullness-benchmarks/libgdx && sed -i '75,77c\  public ModelInstance(final Model model) {
    this.model = model;
    this.transform = new Matrix4();
    copyNodes(model.nodes);
    copyAnimations(model.animations, defaultShareKeyframes);
    calculateTransforms();
  }' gdx/src/com/badlogic/gdx/graphics/g3d/ModelInstance.java && ./gradlew gdx:compileJava -x test -q > new_build_output.log 2>&1 && grep -n "ModelInstance.java:76" new_build_output.log || true
```

